VidFlow Elements & Thumbnail System Implementation
Overview
Build an Elements library where users save, tag, and reference images. The Thumbnail node pulls from this library instead of generating randomly.
Key Features:

Elements Library — Save and tag images
@Mention System — Reference elements in prompts using @tags
Thumbnail Studio Integration — Save generated images to Elements
Thumbnail Node Integration — Use saved elements in pipeline

Image Generation: Gemini Imagen ONLY. No DALL-E, no Flux, no other generators.

Part 1: Database
Elements Table
sqlcreate table elements (
  id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id uuid references auth.users(id) on delete cascade,
  
  name text not null,
  type text not null check (type in ('face', 'product', 'background', 'style', 'thumbnail')),
  tags text[] default '{}',
  
  storage_path text not null,
  thumbnail_path text,
  mime_type text not null,
  file_size int,
  
  metadata jsonb default '{}',
  
  used_count int default 0,
  last_used_at timestamp,
  
  created_at timestamp default now(),
  updated_at timestamp default now()
);

create index idx_elements_user_id on elements(user_id);
create index idx_elements_user_type on elements(user_id, type);
create index idx_elements_tags on elements using gin(tags);
Supabase Storage
Create bucket: elements (public or private based on preference)
Structure:
elements/{user_id}/{uuid}.{ext}
elements/{user_id}/thumbs/{uuid}.{ext}  (smaller preview)

Part 2: API Routes
GET /api/elements
List user's elements with filtering.
Query params:

type — Filter by type (face, product, background, style, thumbnail)
tags — Filter by tags (comma-separated)
search — Search name and tags
limit — Results per page (default 20)
offset — Pagination offset

Response:
json{
  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "uuid",
      "name": "Host Excited",
      "type": "face",
      "tags": ["@host", "@excited"],
      "url": "https://storage.../elements/user/abc.png",
      "thumbnailUrl": "https://storage.../elements/user/thumbs/abc.png",
      "createdAt": "2026-01-06T..."
    }
  ],
  "total": 45,
  "hasMore": true
}
POST /api/elements
Upload new element.
Body: FormData

file — Image file (required)
name — Display name (required)
type — Element type (required)
tags — JSON array of tags (optional)
metadata — JSON object (optional)

Process:

Validate file (image only, max 10MB)
Generate UUID
Upload to Supabase Storage: elements/{user_id}/{uuid}.{ext}
Generate thumbnail (300px max dimension)
Upload thumbnail: elements/{user_id}/thumbs/{uuid}.{ext}
Insert DB record
Return created element

PUT /api/elements/[id]
Update element metadata.
Body:
json{
  "name": "New Name",
  "tags": ["@host", "@casual", "@face"]
}
DELETE /api/elements/[id]
Delete element and storage files.
POST /api/elements/resolve
Resolve @tags to element URLs for pipeline use.
Body:
json{
  "tags": ["@host", "@bg-dark"]
}
Response:
json{
  "resolved": [
    { "tag": "@host", "id": "uuid", "url": "https://...", "type": "face" },
    { "tag": "@bg-dark", "id": "uuid", "url": "https://...", "type": "background" }
  ],
  "missing": []
}
Logic:

For each tag, find element where tags array contains the tag
If multiple matches, use most recently used (last_used_at)
Update used_count and last_used_at for resolved elements

GET /api/elements/tags
List all unique tags the user has used.
Response:
json{
  "tags": ["@host", "@bg-dark", "@product", "@style-neon", "@thumbnail"]
}

